WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
Speaker 1: Welcome to the David Pakman show.&nbsp;
I am Ferron cousins from Ring of Fire with you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:13.120
once again to help close out what has been quite&nbsp;
a crazy week, to put it mildly. So without further&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:18.400
ado. Right. Let's just jump right in to today's&nbsp;
story. No need to waste time. Let's get to it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:26.240
Big story happened this week. The FBI raided&nbsp;
the homes of two individuals involved in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:34.400
Donald Trump's fake elector scheme. Those two&nbsp;
individuals are Brad Carver, who allegedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:40.000
signed a document to be a Trump elector, as well&nbsp;
as Thomas Lane, who worked on Trump's effort to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:47.600
overturn the election in Arizona and New Mexico.&nbsp;
Now, as everybody I'm sure is aware, the DOJ&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:55.280
is, in fact investigating the fake elector&nbsp;
scheme. It's one of the few things from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:00.400
former Trump administration that is actually&nbsp;
being investigated, along with, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:05.920
the 15 boxes of documents that were found down&nbsp;
at Mar a Lago. The DOJ is also investigating that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:13.280
with regard to January six, though, not so much.&nbsp;
We get more to that in just a little bit. But this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:18.320
is a big one, right? We got a fake elector. We got&nbsp;
a guy running Donald Trump's, you know, day to day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:24.480
campaign operations. The FBI raided their homes,&nbsp;
has seized some of their electronic devices.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:31.520
And on top of that, other people also&nbsp;
involved in the scheme have received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:39.840
subpoenas. So here is what this means so&nbsp;
far for this investigation. It just means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:45.520
that it's moving forward. I know that's a&nbsp;
little disappointing. I know nobody ever just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:51.760
wants to hear that the wheels are in motion.&nbsp;
Right. We want action. We want meat. We want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:58.880
something of substance that we can really sink&nbsp;
our teeth into and feel better about these,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:03.920
you know, kind of slow rolling investigations,&nbsp;
which let's be clear, that is what this is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:14.160
I saw a great analysis from a writer this week&nbsp;
that basically said the DOJ is moving too slowly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.320
on this particular story, considering&nbsp;
the fact that this fake elector scheme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.800
didn't just emerge on Tuesday during those&nbsp;
hearings. We've known about it for over a year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.000
And we're just now getting to the point where,&nbsp;
okay, well, these are the fake electors. Now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.320
let's go look in their homes, let's get their&nbsp;
electronic devices. Let's really start to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:42.640
ramp things up a little bit. I guess&nbsp;
whatever it is, it is to slow. But sometimes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:54.160
Sometimes it's slow for a reason. Other times it's&nbsp;
slow. Out of abundance of caution. And I'm afraid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.160 --> 00:03:01.680
that is the situation that we are looking at right&nbsp;
now. The DOJ, led by a course Attorney General&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:08.960
Merrick Garland, doesn't want to give any kind of&nbsp;
appearance that they were being overtly political.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.320
They want to make sure that they have&nbsp;
crossed their T's and dotted their eyes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:24.000
before they make any moves on anyone. Even some&nbsp;
of these low level individuals. But even still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:29.680
sometimes when you have the evidence, you don't&nbsp;
need to sit on it. You don't need the weight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:35.920
You don't need to hold off on issuing subpoenas&nbsp;
until the public is squarely in your corner.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:42.400
Sometimes you have to do something, even if&nbsp;
it's unpopular, if it is the right thing to do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:47.760
And I do believe that that, of course, is the&nbsp;
situation that we're looking at right now with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.840
the fake elector scheme. I mean, after&nbsp;
all, that is one of the biggest things.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.720 --> 00:04:00.080
Obviously, there is so much with January six than&nbsp;
with the January six committee and all of that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:05.200
that we could probably pop a lot of people for a&nbsp;
lot of different crimes right away. Trump, himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:10.720
included. And again, I'm going to get to that in&nbsp;
just a few moments. But. This fake elector scheme.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:17.120
This was the big gambit, right? They knew&nbsp;
that their court cases were losing. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:23.360
knew they didn't have evidence of voter fraud.&nbsp;
But they pushed ahead with all of this anyway.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:31.120
And in some states, yeah, they had people ready&nbsp;
to go in Michigan. We found out this week that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:37.520
they're fake elector scheme because the electors&nbsp;
had to be in the state capital to cast their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:43.520
votes. So what they had planned, which of course,&nbsp;
didn't come to fruition, but they had planned to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:50.880
somehow sneak into the Michigan state capital&nbsp;
so that they would be present the following day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:58.480
to be able to cast their fake Electoral College&nbsp;
vote. I mean, that is how deep this scheme went.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:06.000
I mean, this truly is, you know, cross-country.&nbsp;
You know, north to south, south, east to west,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:12.400
all over the country. You had these little&nbsp;
fake electors willing to do whatever it took.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:19.200
To make Donald Trump the winner of the election.&nbsp;
So thank goodness, of course, that we do have the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:25.760
DOJ investigating this. You know, thank goodness&nbsp;
we're seeing some of these positive step forward.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:31.360
Individuals do need to be subpoenaed. They do&nbsp;
need to you know, if they're not going to comply,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:36.160
if we think they might hide or destroy evidence,&nbsp;
they do have to be raided. That's how that works.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:41.360
That's why, by the way, that typically works&nbsp;
in that manner. If you have an individual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:46.480
you think could destroy evidence, could be&nbsp;
hiding things, that's when you send the FBI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:53.600
in to go try to find it. Now, over in Georgia as&nbsp;
well, the fake elector scheme has been gaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.600 --> 00:06:01.520
steam and we have seen in recent weeks several of&nbsp;
the people who signed on to be the fake electors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:07.520
not, of course, necessarily in a criminal&nbsp;
way. And what I mean by that is you do have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:13.840
some of the people who were the, quote, fake&nbsp;
electors in Georgia that are fully cooperating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:19.120
with the investigators because they said, listen,&nbsp;
I was approached with this and they said if these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:24.800
court cases overturn everything for Donald Trump,&nbsp;
we're going to need our electors. Are you willing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:29.360
to do that? And so you had plenty of people in the&nbsp;
state of Georgia, these Republicans, who said, oh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:35.280
yeah, we'll do it if, if and only if these court&nbsp;
cases overturn the election. I'm here ready to go.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.600
And then once the court case is lost, these&nbsp;
people said, all right, I'm out. I'm not going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:46.320
do this. And those people have been working with&nbsp;
these investigators both in Georgia and the feds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.680
And more importantly, they've&nbsp;
been giving them names.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:54.720
They said, Listen, I'm more than willing to talk&nbsp;
to you, but I'm probably not the guy you need.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.960
You need, you know, this person, this person in&nbsp;
this person, the names have not been released.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:05.760
So they are getting better leads. And the more&nbsp;
leads you get, the longer the investigation takes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:10.160
the more people you have to question, the more&nbsp;
people you have to subpoena. And of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:15.840
you have to go to the courts to get the subpoenas.&nbsp;
So maybe it's being slow rolled out of that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:21.920
abundance of caution, which I do believe&nbsp;
is the driving factor. But it also could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:30.240
that there's just so many different leads, so&nbsp;
many different states, so many different players&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:38.800
that this investigation kind of has to go&nbsp;
slow. Because you don't want to miss anyone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:45.760
And sometimes in our impatience and I'll admit&nbsp;
I'm probably public enemy number one on that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:52.960
Sometimes we forget about that. You know, we&nbsp;
all want this kind of instant gratification with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:59.440
these investigations. And unfortunately, that's&nbsp;
just not the way it works. So we do have to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:06.080
patient. We do have to let the process play itself&nbsp;
out because there are far too many players here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:12.880
For us to even admit, ignore&nbsp;
or forget a single one of them

